---
import SiteLayout from '../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const href = (value: string) => `${base.replace(/\/?$/, '/')}${value.replace(/^\/+/, '')}`;
const flow = 'Benchmark assets: Package / Case / RunVariant\n' +
  '                  │\n' +
  '                  ▼\n' +
  'Evaluation Engine: validate → resolve → preview → freeze\n' +
  '                  │\n' +
  '                  ▼\n' +
  'Immutable EvaluationTask → ExecutionAttempt(s)\n' +
  '                  │\n' +
  '                  ▼\n' +
  'Evidence → validity check → EvaluationResult\n' +
  '                  │\n' +
  '                  ▼\n' +
  'Reporting / aggregation / regression analysis';
---
<SiteLayout title="Sandbox Benchmark Architecture" lang="en" description="Sandbox Benchmark evaluation flow, reading paths, and current reliability evaluation scope.">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Sandbox / Evaluation</span>
    <h1>Benchmark architecture and evaluation boundaries</h1>
    <p>A Benchmark states what claim should be tested, runs a traceable experiment, and produces a result from valid evidence. This page is the overall map and reading guide; Case semantics, task freezing, and result adjudication are defined by their respective owner documents.</p>
    <div class="home-actions">
      <a href={href('/components/sandbox/#benchmark-framework-en')}>Evaluation framework and CUT boundaries <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/components/ca-benchmarks/#benchmark-assets-en')}>Benchmark assets and Cases <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/components/ca-benchmark-engine/#evaluation-lifecycle-en')}>Execution lifecycle and result semantics <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Evaluation flow</h2>
    <pre><code>{flow}</code></pre>
    <p>Freeze fixes the inputs and resolved bindings for an evaluation. It does not start execution, and it does not guarantee that the trial will be valid or pass.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Three questions, three authoritative definitions</h2>
    <div class="reading-list">
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/components/sandbox/#benchmark-framework-en')}>
        <span class="reading-number">01</span>
        <span><strong>What are we trying to prove?</strong><small>The Sandbox-level evaluation framework describes claims, Component Under Test (CUT) boundaries, evaluation directions, and applicable modes.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/components/ca-benchmarks/#benchmark-assets-en')}>
        <span class="reading-number">02</span>
        <span><strong>What exactly is evaluated?</strong><small>The Benchmark asset repository defines Packages, Cases, RunVariants, expected semantics, and Case-specific evidence. The owner repository is authoritative for the first 13 Cases and their status.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/components/ca-benchmark-engine/#evaluation-lifecycle-en')}>
        <span class="reading-number">03</span>
        <span><strong>How is it executed and judged?</strong><small>The Engine defines resolution and freezing, ExecutionAttempts, evidence validity, EvaluationResults, and reporting boundaries.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Current focus: reliability</h2>
    <p>Current priorities include constraint adherence, authoritative outcome verification, handling unknown results, safe recovery, and evidence validity. These are evaluation directions, not a complete Case inventory; they do not imply that every Case, Mode, or Environment realization has passed live acceptance.</p>
    <p><a href={href('/components/sandbox/#benchmark-framework-en')}>Read the owner-maintained evaluation directions and boundaries →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>A result is more than PASS / FAIL</h2>
    <p>An evaluation report must distinguish CUT behavior, authoritative Environment state, whether the evidence supports a judgment, and the final Benchmark Verdict. Environment or evaluation-infrastructure failures must not automatically be attributed to the CUT; the Engine and Case contracts define the specific rules.</p>
    <p><a href={href('/runbooks/real-5gc/')}>Read the real 5GC runbook and acceptance evidence →</a></p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
